description:
PR group S2: one site PR. It may be stacked on the unmerged S1 PR.

Build `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` with `concurrency: pages-deploy` and cancel-in-progress false. Triggers: push to main, repository_dispatch `core-bundle`, and workflow_dispatch with mode deploy, redeploy or rollback, plus a receipt run id for rollback.

1. Resolve. Pick the bundle: the dispatch payload, or the newest certified bundle for a push. Fail closed unless all of these hold:
   - the digest matches;
   - schema is N or N-1;
   - certified_by is a successful trunk.yml push run on core_sha;
   - every attestation passed, or was skipped with a recorded reason;
   - core_sha is not older than the deployed one: `GET /repos/BenchBox-dev/BenchBox/compare/{deployed}...{core_sha}` returns `ahead` or `identical`. Any 403, 404 or 5xx fails closed.
   - if corpus_sha changed, validator_parity's base equals the deployed core_sha.
2. Build from the bundle with SITE_ORIGIN and SITE_HOST. When SITE_DEPLOY_TARGET is `rehearsal`, every page gets noindex and robots.txt disallows all.
3. Gates, in TypeScript under deploy/. Each port is tested against the Python check's fixtures, copied as JSON:
   - privacy on the artifact;
   - links (internal links and fragments, with inventory/known-broken-links.json);
   - explorer_compat: the built Explorer and the previously deployed Explorer (read-model version taken from the deployed receipt) both support contract.json;
   - snapshot_digest: if corpus_sha is unchanged, the snapshot sha256 equals the deployed one;
   - origin: no https://benchbox.dev in a rehearsal artifact outside the allowlist.
4. Deploy with actions/deploy-pages, only when vars.SITE_DEPLOY_TARGET is `rehearsal` or `production`.
5. Probe every route class and compare the served bytes with the artifact digests (a port of verify_live.py).
6. Write a receipt JSON: site sha, core_sha, bundle digest, artifact sha256, Explorer read-model version, deployment id, gate and probe results, queue time and core-merge-to-live latency. Store it as a 90-day artifact and in the deployment status.
7. On failure:
   - resolve, build or gate failure on a core-bundle trigger: open or update one core issue labelled `site-bundle-failed`;
   - probe failure after deploy: if a receipt with green probes exists and this run is not a rollback, dispatch exactly one rollback run to it, then open the issue. A failing rollback never triggers another; it opens an issue and stops.

Unit tests must cover: stale, unverifiable and chain-broken bundles; every gate; receipts; rollback with no green receipt; rollback of a rollback; and overlapping runs in both orders.
